I've added the test for #1181 and committed it (d09a31a6). All 8 rows already pass on HEAD with yoagent 0.27.8, so no product code changed. One thing to know first: the commit title still says "azure" and "headers credential", but neither of those rows could be tested, because yoyo has no azure provider and no config headers key.

The test. The new file is tests/provider_redirect_canary.rs. It runs the built binary with a fake key and a scrubbed environment against two stubs on 127.0.0.1. Stub A answers every request with a 307 or 302 pointing at stub B, and stub B records every request it gets.

| row | requests to A | requests to B | exit | stderr |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| anthropic × 307 / 302 | 1 | 0 | 1 | yoagent's refusal, naming B's address as "outside" A's |
| google × 307 / 302 | 1 | 0 | 1 | same, prefixed Google: |
| openai × 307 / 302 | 1 | 0 | 1 | same |
| openrouter × 307 / 302 | 1 | 0 | 1 | same |

Nothing retries the refusal, and the user sees yoagent's own message. The generic "API error with no fallback configured" line comes after it rather than replacing it, so src/prompt_retry.rs didn't need a fix.

Two of the owner's rows don't exist in yoyo:
• azure: create_model_config has no azure branch. An unknown provider name falls back to the generic OpenAI-compatible setup, which the openai row covers.
• a credential in config `headers`: no config key fills ModelConfig::headers. yoyo only puts its own client headers there, so I used openrouter (the provider with the most of them) for that path.

Whether to add either as a feature is a separate decision. I've said so on #1181.

Checks that the test can fail:
• Pointing each provider straight at stub B, the stub recorded the request, the key and the body, so its zeros in the matrix mean something.
• I temporarily made yoyo treat every error as retriable, then restored it in the same command. Every row then failed by name, with A receiving 6 requests instead of 1.

OpenAPI (read only, not run): yoyo builds its OpenAPI tools with no auth (src/agent_builder.rs:689), so no yoyo credential goes out with them. There was nothing to file upstream.

Build, the full test suite, clippy and fmt all pass. The 8-row table is posted on #1181 ahead of the push that closes it.
